      "text-diff": {
        "ui": {
          "r62_0": "Paste the original text here",
          "r62_1": "Paste the modified text here",
          "r62_2": "Compare the two texts and highlight differences",
          "r62_3": "Original text",
          "r62_4": "Modified text",
          "r62_5": "Unified diff output",
          "r62_6": "Ignore whitespace",
          "r62_7": "Ignore case",
          "r62_8": "compares words and the whitespace between them, so a one-word edit in a long paragraph shows as one word instead of a whole changed line. Best for prose and prompts.",
          "r62_9": "compares single characters (Unicode code points, so emoji and accented letters count as one). Best for short strings such as IDs, hashes, or URLs.",
          "r6_0": "<span class=\"w-3 h-3 bg-success-100 border border-success-300 rounded-sm\"></span> Added",
          "r6_1": "<span class=\"w-3 h-3 bg-error-100 border border-error-300 rounded-sm\"></span> Removed",
          "r6_2": "Added",
          "r6_3": "Removed",
          "r6_4": "Unchanged",
          "r6_5": "<span class=\"material-symbols-rounded\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-icon=\"content_copy\"></span> Copy diff",
          "r6_6": "<span class=\"material-symbols-rounded\" aria-hidden=\"true\" data-icon=\"download\"></span> Download .diff",
          "r6_7": "The diff uses Myers' algorithm, which finds a shortest edit script: the fewest insertions and deletions that turn the original into the modified text. Everything else is shown as unchanged. All of it runs in your browser. For very large inputs that share little text, the search is capped to keep the page responsive; the page tells you when that happens, and the diff it shows is still correct but may not be the smallest one.",
          "r6_8": "<strong>Lines</strong> compares whole lines, like <code>diff</code> and <code>git diff</code>. Best for code, config files, and logs.",
          "r6_9": "<strong>Ignore case</strong> treats upper- and lower-case letters as equal.",
          "r6_10": "<strong>Ignore whitespace</strong> in line mode removes all spaces, tabs, and other whitespace before comparing two lines, like <code>git diff -w</code>, so re-indented lines count as unchanged. In word and character modes, any run of whitespace matches any other run, so <code>a&nbsp;&nbsp;b</code> matches <code>a b</code>, but whitespace added where there was none still counts as a change.",
          "r6_11": "The export uses the unified format that <code>diff -u</code> produces and <code>patch</code> reads:",
          "r6_12": "<code>---</code> and <code>+++</code> name the original and modified files.",
          "r6_13": "Each hunk starts with <code>@@ -start,count +start,count @@</code>: the first line number and the number of lines the hunk covers in each file. A count of 1 is left out.",
          "r6_14": "Lines starting with a space are context, <code>-</code> lines are removed, and <code>+</code> lines are added. Each hunk has up to 3 lines of context, and changes that close together share a hunk.",
          "r6_15": "<code>\\ No newline at end of file</code> marks a last line that has no trailing newline.",
          "r6_16": "To apply the downloaded file: <code>patch original.txt text-diff.diff</code>.",
          "r6_17": "With an ignore option on, lines that count as equal are written as context from the original text. Applying that patch does not reproduce the ignored differences.",
          "r6_18": "<strong>Config files:</strong> compare a deployed <code>.env</code>, YAML, or nginx config with the version you expect, and turn on ignore whitespace to hide indentation noise.",
          "r6_19": "<strong>LLM prompt versions:</strong> use word mode to see exactly which instructions changed between two prompt drafts before you compare model outputs.",
          "r6_20": "<strong>Code review:</strong> paste two versions of a function to read the change outside your editor, or export a <code>.diff</code> to attach to an issue or a message."
        }
      },
